<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The points <m>A({1},\,{-4},\,{5})</m>, <m>B({5},\,{-4},\,{-4})</m> and <m>C({4},\,{-2},\,{-2})</m> are three corners of a parallelogram.</p><p>Give the coordinates of a point D so that A, B, C and D, in some order, are the four corners of a parallelogram. (There is more than one correct answer.)</p><div>D = ( <fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> )   </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal vectors. For ABCD, <m>\overrightarrow{AD} = \overrightarrow{BC}</m>, so <m>\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{a} + (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b})</m>, which gives D<m>({0},\,{-2},\,{7})</m>.</p><p>The other two choices put D opposite C (parallelogram ACBD, <m>\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}</m>), giving <m>({2},\,{-6},\,{3})</m>, or opposite A (parallelogram ABDC, <m>\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}</m>), giving <m>({8},\,{-2},\,{-11})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>0</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>7</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>